576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 389 0 R
/E (In the Clothing Size Predictor project, the KNN stages begin with collecting data containing age, weight, height, and clothing size. The data is then cleaned from missing values and outliers, and normalized. After selecting the optimal K value, the Euclidean distance is calculated to identify the nearest neighbors. The clothing size is predicted based on the majority of these neighbors, and the model is evaluated using accuracy and a confusion matrix to ensure prediction performance.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
