609 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 391 0 R
/E (In this project, data preprocessing is conducted before applying KNN or other models. First, the dataset is loaded from final_test.csv, containing features age, weight, height and target size. Missing values in age, height, and weight are filled using the median, and outliers are removed using the z-score method. The size column is mapped from strings \(XXS, S, M, L, XL, XXL, XXXL\) to numeric values for model compatibility. Additional features such as BMI \(body-mass index\) and weight-squared are created to improve prediction effectiveness. Finally, all features are normalized to ensure balanced scaling, and the dataset is split into training set \(90%\) and testing set \(10%\) for model training and evaluation.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
