/E (The code on the slide shows the complete process of machine learning modeling, starting from dividing the dataset into features \(X\) and targets \(Y\), then separating the data into train and test data, followed by storing several algorithms such as Logistic Regression, KNN, Naive Bayes, and Decision Tree into a dictionary for easy comparison. The fit_and_score function is used to train each model and calculate its accuracy on the test data, so we can see which model is the best. In addition, an example of the use of Decision Tree is shown in more detail by retraining, making predictions, and displaying a confusion matrix to understand the quality of the predictions in more depth.)
